1. A method performed by a docking center, the method comprising:

   detecting a dockee requesting access to a peripheral device connected to the docking center;

   providing, to the dockee, connection information usable by the dockee to establish a direct wireless connection with the peripheral device;

   facilitating establishment of the direct wireless connection between the dockee and the peripheral device based at least in part on the connection information, such that data communication between the dockee and the peripheral device is performed without routing the data communication through the docking center;

   after facilitating establishment of the direct wireless connection, discovering a second wireless group formed by the dockee, wherein the dockee operates as a group owner of the second wireless group; and

   joining, by the docking center, the second wireless group as a client of the dockee.

A docking center apparatus comprising one or more processors configured to:

receive, from a dockee device, a request for information enabling a direct connection between the dockee device and a peripheral device;

provide, to the dockee device, direct connection information associated with the peripheral device;

receive, from the dockee device, an assist request associated with establishing the direct connection between the dockee device and the peripheral device;

in response to the assist request, release an existing connection between the docking center apparatus and the peripheral device;

cease control of the peripheral device; and

join a communication group of the dockee device as a client device,

wherein the docking center apparatus remains a group owner of a separate communication group while operating as the client device in the communication group of the dockee device.
